{"id":"perfc-tests","ord":"aD","title":"Testing & CI","created":"2026-08-21T13:01:43-04:00"}
{"id":"transcript-stream-quadratic","parent":"perfc-server","ord":"a3","title":"Chat streaming is quadratic in bytes AND stop-and-wait (one frame per round trip) — a 15 kB answer costs more wire than the whole app","done":"2026-08-22T12:48:48-04:00","desc":"**Symptom:** chat answers stream in slow, lumpy pulses from kolu-bot (India) to a laptop (Canada) over a DIRECT tailnet (~250ms RTT; DERP ruled out via `tailscale status`).\\n\\n**Measured two ways — ACP chunk counts on kolu-bot, and a full browser+websocket instrument over an artificial delayed TCP link (scratchpad: chatwire.ts, proxy.ts, stream-agent.ts). Two independent defects:**\\n\\n**1. Quadratic bytes (every agent, every link).** The chat rebuilds the whole accumulated string and upserts the FULL row per chunk (transcript.ts:428 `#grow` → runtime.ts:1067 upsert), and kolu's coalescer is a `queueMicrotask` latch (kolu server.ts:713) that merges nothing because ACP chunks arrive on separate I/O ticks — one frame per chunk, each carrying the entire answer so far. Frame k ≈ k·chunk + ~190B envelope. Amplification ≈ chunks/2:\\n- opencode on kolu-bot: 3.2 kB answer → 643 chunks (~5B each) → **1.04 MB on the wire, 323×.**\\n- synthetic 800-chunk answer (37.9 kB) → **15.0 MB, 406×.**\\n- real Claude adapter, 14.6 kB answer → 843 kB — **more wire than loading the ENTIRE app** (HTML+JS+fonts+icons = 777 kB the same session).\\n\\n**2. Stop-and-wait: exactly one frame per round trip (unexpected, bigger on a long link).** The transcript stream ACKs each frame with a hard-coded credit window of 1 (effect RpcServer/RpcClient `supportsAck`), and kolu builds streaming members with `Stream.fromAsyncIterable` (kolu server.ts:372,409) — the NON-coalescing Effect branch — so each round trip carries one delta, never the batch accumulated during it. Time = chunks × RTT, independent of bandwidth (capping the link to 5 Mbps cost 8%; it ran 93% idle). At RTT 200ms, a 400-chunk answer the agent finished in 10.6s took **82.6s to finish arriving — the panel 72s behind, painting at 5 chunks/s.** 800 chunks: 147s behind.\\n- **When it bites:** any agent streaming faster than ~5 chunks/s at 200ms RTT. The pinned Claude adapter batches (~1.4 chunks/s) so it stays hidden today — the long-haul Claude run showed ZERO lag. opencode and every token-level streamer land at 20–40 chunks/s and hit the wall immediately, which is exactly the human's report.\\n\\n**Fix, cheapest first (the measurement ranks them):**\\n1. Throttle transcript.say / chat.ts:434 so chunks in one tick collapse before publish — kolu's existing microtask coalescer then genuinely merges them. Fixes BOTH defects, no protocol change. Start here.\\n2. Give the row an append representation (a chunk delta carries only its new text) — fixes bytes to O(N), independent of (1).\\n3. Make the transcript member produce via the Effect/Queue shape instead of `Stream.fromAsyncIterable` so a round trip carries the whole accumulated batch — fixes the RTT stall; a kolu-side change.\\n- Browser appends and throttles the Markdown re-render to match.\\n\\n**Not this node:** kimi-k3 via LiteLLM from India was also slow at the model level (first token 7.3s) — provider latency, separate from the wire.","created":"2026-08-22T08:39:49-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T12:48:48-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-22 (slow streaming, Canada↔India direct tailnet); measured on kolu-bot","kolu-pr":"fix 3 = juspay/kolu#2202 (re-land of #2199 with a bounded Stream.buffer(512, suspend) + settle-based membership tests), MERGED 2026-08-22 12:36 as 020f05af with all ci:: contexts green on both platforms (history: #2199 merged 8b9820ed without odu — orchestrator error — found red, reverted via #2201 = 9a1137b8); olai's pin moves to 020f05af in #345","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/345 — merged 2026-08-22 as d6f80e78 (fixes 1+2, pin to kolu 020f05af) + https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2202 — merged as 020f05af (fix 3). Measured: 1,118 kB/643 frames → 19.6 kB/82 loopback; 1,093 kB → 18.6 kB over a 200 ms relay. The panel-behind number was not reproduced by the lane's relay instrument (0.2 s behind before) — verify on the real Canada↔India link after deploy."}}
{"id":"psw2-server","parent":"perf-sweep-2026-08-19","ord":"a6","title":"Server: every open tab pays for every keystroke","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:29:55-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-streams-per-tab","parent":"psw2-server","ord":"a0","title":"Five page answers are rebuilt on every write — once per open tab","done":"2026-08-25T10:05:44-04:00","desc":"The page, filter, calendar, overdue and move-picker answers are each wired as a poll stream, and the framework runs one full recompute loop PER SUBSCRIBED TAB, fired by every write (runtime.ts:967-1020). The \"did anything change?\" comparison runs AFTER the rebuild — it saves the network frame, never the work — and each read also spins a fresh fiber and, on the nothing-changed path, still walks the whole answer structurally to say so. So three tabs on the same page = three identical rebuilds per keystroke.\n\nFix shape: compute once per revision per distinct question and share the result across subscribers; find a cheap \"could this have changed?\" test that runs before the rebuild, not after.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T10:05:44-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","brief":"briefs/pst.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25 07:58 (sweep campaign wave 1, the human's word)","merge":"AUTO (the human 07:57): grok review folded + CI green; gate = per-subscriber delta-equivalence harness + pre-check mutation proof","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/387 — MERGED 09fbd710","worktree":".worktrees/streams-per-tab"}}
{"id":"perf-git-per-write","parent":"psw2-server","ord":"a1","title":"Git is consulted about every uncommitted file on every write — and the bill grows until you commit","done":"2026-08-25T09:08:39-04:00","desc":"Every revision runs `git status`, and then for EVERY dirty outline a `git show HEAD:<file>` subprocess plus a full parse of the old copy, to build the node-level diff (runtime.ts:617, pending.ts:800-860). Under manual commit the dirty list only grows during a session, so typing literally gets slower the longer a commit is deferred. The comment admits only \"one git status on a clean directory\".\n\nFix shape: HEAD's copy of a file cannot change between commits — cache the parsed old copy per (commit, file); or compute the detailed diff only when the Commit UI actually asks for it.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T09:08:39-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","brief":"briefs/pgw.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25 07:58 (sweep campaign wave 1)","merge":"AUTO (the human 07:57): pi review folded + CI green; gate = scripted-git-session reference-arm test + O(changed) subprocess count","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/385 — MERGED 74c71eab","worktree":".worktrees/git-per-write"}}
{"id":"psw2-model","parent":"perf-sweep-2026-08-19","ord":"a7","title":"The model: costs that grow with the vault's age","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:30:01-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-agenda-history-walk","parent":"psw2-model","ord":"a0","title":"The overdue count walks every past day — and fully dresses every overdue item — to produce two numbers","done":"2026-08-25T09:02:25-04:00","desc":"behind() visits every day before today and builds the complete entry for each overdue node (parent trail, blockers, progress) even though the subscriber only wants two counts; recomputed per revision (agenda.ts:348-399, ops query.ts:588). The forward walk and the calendar likewise skip LINEARLY over every earlier day instead of jumping to the start (agenda.ts:398, dates.ts:92). A vault with years of journal days pays for all of them on every write.\n\nFix shape: maintain the two counts as an index the patcher keeps (the dated-index precedent), and start day-walks with a sorted lookup instead of a skip.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T09:02:25-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","brief":"briefs/pah.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25 07:58 (sweep campaign wave 1)","merge":"AUTO (the human 07:57): grok review folded + CI green; gate = counts≡walk differential + the midnight/mark-done boundary pins","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/386 — MERGED e914a6c2","worktree":".worktrees/agenda-history-walk"}}
{"id":"perf-key-resort","parent":"psw2-model","ord":"a1","title":"Editing near a popular tag re-sorts that tag's whole vault-wide list","done":"2026-08-25T10:22:06-04:00","desc":"When a patch touches a key, the patcher rebuilds that key's ENTIRE member list — copy plus re-sort — even though only a few members moved (patch.ts:380-388). Typing in any file that mentions #kitchen re-sorts every #kitchen record in the vault; same for a busy day in byDay or a large parent's children. The header's \"bounded by the touched file\" claim covers the folds above this line, not this rebuild.\n\nFix shape: splice into the already-sorted list instead of copying and re-sorting it.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T10:22:06-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","brief":"briefs/pkr.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25 09:09 (sweep queue #4; trigger met: #385's merge freed the slot)","merge":"AUTO: pi review folded + CI green; gate = spliced≡rebuilt differential + one-position-off mutation proof","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/389 — MERGED 73a63a10","worktree":".worktrees/key-resort"}}
{"id":"perf-overlay-copies","parent":"psw2-model","ord":"a2","title":"The patcher copies its carried bookkeeping even when a patch doesn't touch it","done":"2026-08-25T11:15:54-04:00","desc":"Each layered index deep-copies its carried layer in the constructor — three copies — and then throws them away untouched if the patch wrote nothing to that index (overlay.ts:280-333). The layer may grow to half the corpus before flattening, so a long editing session pays up to 3 × n/2 copies × 6 indexes per keystroke for nothing.\n\nFix shape: copy lazily, on the first actual write to the layer.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T11:15:54-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","brief":"briefs/poc.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25 10:23 (sweep queue #6; the slot freed by #389's merge)","merge":"AUTO: pi review folded + CI green; gate = the aliasing pin + every existing differential untouched-green","merged":"bc886435","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/392","worktree":".worktrees/overlay-copies"}}
{"id":"perf-doc-backlinks-index","parent":"psw2-model","ord":"a3","title":"A document's page re-scans every link in every file, on every write","done":"2026-08-25T11:37:38-04:00","desc":"\"What links to this document?\" has no reverse index — referrersTo loops over every face in the directory and tests every link (backlinks.ts:242-275), per revision, per tab sitting on any .md/.html page. The node-to-node direction next door IS indexed; this is the one direction that isn't, and the comment admits it.\n\nFix shape: one more maintained index, links → documents, kept by the patcher like the others.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T11:37:38-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","brief":"briefs/pdb.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25 10:06 (sweep queue #5; the slot freed by #387's merge)","merge":"AUTO: grok review folded + CI green; gate = index≡scan differential + maintenance mutation proof","merged":"52ba0f81","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/393","worktree":".worktrees/doc-backlinks-index"}}
{"id":"perf-filename-conventions","parent":"psw2-model","ord":"a5","title":"Pins and the inbox re-derive their by-filename answers on every write","todo":true,"desc":"Every revision re-allocates the full file list, lowercases every basename and re-sorts, for answers that only change when a file is added, removed or renamed (shelf.ts:192, inbox.ts:99, runtime.ts:671-716). The cell equality swallows the frame, not the work.\n\nFix shape: recompute only when the set of file paths actually changed.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T07:56:25-04:00","custom":{"dispatch-trigger":"sweep queue #7: Opus slot free — Opus, reviewer grok, AUTO; recompute only on path-set change"}}
{"id":"psw2-ops","parent":"perf-sweep-2026-08-19","ord":"aA","title":"Ops: tool calls that touch everything","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:30:20-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-capture-paths","parent":"psw2-ops","ord":"a0","title":"capture builds every node in the vault just to learn the list of filenames","doing":true,"desc":"Resolving where a capture lands calls the full outlines listing, which materializes and filters every node in the directory, only for the file paths to be kept (ops query.ts:967-1024, tools.ts:310) — paid per capture, sometimes twice via the retry wrapper.\n\nFix shape: a paths-only question; the listing keeps its counts for list_outlines, which genuinely needs them.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T11:17:09-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","brief":"briefs/pob.md","dispatched":"2026-08-25T11:18:00-04:00","merge":"auto","worktree":".worktrees/ops-walks"}}
{"id":"perf-batch-assemble","parent":"psw2-ops","ord":"a1","title":"The batch context: one asking per batch, one planner per op — plan.ts's braid unwinds and the O(files)-per-op cost dies in the same diff","doing":true,"desc":"One change with two faces — the performance fix and the Hickey refactor are the same diff, which is the sign the seam is real (ruled with the human 2026-08-25).\n\n**The performance face (the original finding):** the batch fold rebuilds the full document set — fresh map, full path sort — once per op, so a 100-op batch pays it 100 times (following.ts:135, set.ts:152/304; the header admits it). Beside it, every write that names a file does a LINEAR find over all served paths (refusals.ts:207 via plan.ts:440 and friends), and the broken-files map is rebuilt at ~8 call sites per single write.\n\n**The Hickey face:** plan.ts (4,646 lines, ~2,500 of code — the vault's biggest file) fails the braid test not by length but by complecting three things: DECIDING what an op means, ASKING the set the same questions over and over (the 8 call sites above), and SEQUENCING the batch. File size is the shadow; the interleaving is the smell. (filter.ts and derive.ts pass the same test — big but single-braided; they stay.)\n\n**The one diff, three moves:**\n1. A `PlanningContext` value — assembled set, paths-as-a-Set, broken map, homes — computed ONCE per batch and passed in. The 8 re-asks die; path lookup becomes a map hit; the per-op O(files log files) becomes per-batch.\n2. Each op's planner becomes an independent pure function `(context, op) → plan`, dispatched by a map — the shape TOOLS already has one layer up. Whether plan.ts is then one file or eight is an editorial choice, not architecture.\n3. Plans stay data (they already are — refusals and writes as values), which is what makes the moves behavior-preserving.\n\n**Not the goal:** splitting files for line count's sake. After the decomplect, filing is free to follow taste.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T11:46:50-04:00","custom":{"bundled-in":"perf-capture-paths"}}
{"id":"perf-homes-files","parent":"psw2-ops","ord":"a2","title":"Every fold click rebuilds two all-files structures — under a comment claiming it doesn't","doing":true,"desc":"homes builds a fresh Set of every outline path and a fresh broken-files Map per call (ops query.ts:533-534), and the browser calls it once per fold/unfold. The doc block above it asserts \"neither half is a walk\" — the id half is indeed a lookup; the file half is O(all files) per click.\n\nFix shape: hold both structures with the snapshot they describe; fix the comment either way.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T11:17:09-04:00","custom":{"bundled-in":"perf-capture-paths"}}
{"id":"perf-didyoumean","parent":"psw2-ops","ord":"a3","title":"Every refused reference runs a similarity check against every id in the vault","doing":true,"desc":"\"Did you mean…\" walks all ids per unresolved reference — per refused edit from a stale tab, per bad id in a broken file, per armed chat chip (refusals.ts:75, suggest.ts:24, edit.ts, context.ts:81). Partly admitted; harmless one at a time, unbounded when a stale tab replays a burst of refusals.\n\nFix shape: cap the candidates (e.g. by length bucket) or compute suggestions lazily, only when a person will actually see them.","created":"2026-08-24T16:28:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T11:17:09-04:00","custom":{"bundled-in":"perf-capture-paths"}}
{"id":"sidx-implement","parent":"search-index","ord":"a0","title":"implement + open PR + bench + PAUSE for the human's manual test","done":"2026-08-24T20:12:59-04:00","desc":"PAUSE POINT reached 20:12 (terminal a41b4aac, 1h08m): PR #374 @ cca1b21. The index: incremental from what a write touched, one matcher grammar (unindexable operators filter the index's candidate set through the existing matcher), lazy cold build once per process (114.1ms on the bench corpus). Bench (1,000 outlines / 21,552 records / 200 docs / 0.77MB prose): typical queries 15-21× (14.9ms→0.87ms), miss 69×, and an honest DECLINE heuristic — a crowd query (19,600 hits) answers by walk at 0.9× parity because the index there would be 22ms, genuinely slower. Maintenance: 1.03ms median for a 21-record file rewrite, 0.36ms no-op revision. Bar: typecheck 16/16, 3624/0 + 77 unit, e2e 917/7947 all passing. CI 10/10 @ cca1b21. Flagged not deferred: master's architecture.md describes the PARKED semantic-recall index (packages/server/src/recall/, an ops Recall seam) that is not in the tree — unmerged-branch text, left for the orchestrator/human. HOLDING for the human's manual test; reviews (grok+pi) start on their word.","created":"2026-08-24T19:02:23-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T20:12:59-04:00","custom":{"pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/374 @ cca1b21","terminal":"a41b4aac"}}
{"id":"sidx-review-grok","parent":"search-index","ord":"a1","title":"review: grok (split) — after the human's manual test","done":"2026-08-24T20:28:27-04:00","desc":"grok, DO-NOT-OBJECT, 0 MUST, at cca1b21 (20:28, 10m49s, by reading; one surgical probe on FTS5-trigram-vs-JS-substring semantics) — https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/374#issuecomment-5403302722. Concurrency judged sound (the event loop serializes a write or a second query around the cold build). Three non-blocking notes, converging with pi: the soak never crosses CROWD_FLOOR; a few write shapes are traced rather than soaked; the bench does not state memory.","after":["sidx-implement"],"created":"2026-08-24T19:02:23-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T20:28:27-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"grok","terminal":"79b380df"}}
{"id":"sidx-review-pi","parent":"search-index","ord":"a2","title":"review: pi (split) — after the human's manual test","done":"2026-08-24T20:26:39-04:00","desc":"pi, DO-NOT-OBJECT, 1 SHOULD, 2 NIT, at cca1b21 (20:26, ~10m, by reading; 'one surgical probe was allowed; none was needed') — https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/374#issuecomment-5403282539. All six axes verified: STALENESS clean — the index updates in the same table as the Reading it answers from (no publisher window); every write shape rides the probe-stamp → codec-delta → patcher channel or is derived state the matcher re-evaluates; the one corpus where candidates and walk could differ (duplicate ids) is the corpus the validator refuses. Differential test: full-answer comparisons incl. order/withDesc/totals/cap, candidate-superset asserted; two gaps (soak never crosses CROWD_FLOOR; mirror churn untested) judged safe by construction. Decline heuristic: bounded lookup (crowd+1), measured threshold, can only choose the safe path. One-matcher: no second spelling; edge cases fall toward over-inclusion or refusal, never a lost hit. Concurrency: synchronous SQLite, single thread — cold build atomic. SHOULD (the one real finding): MEMORY unstated — the brainstorm priced FTS5 trigram postings ~3× text on disk, the implementation moved them onto the long-lived Bun heap, and neither bench nor README says the per-record cost. NITs: bench's why column re-spells the trigram floor in UTF-16 units; query.ts doc comment misattributes the soak.","after":["sidx-implement"],"created":"2026-08-24T19:02:23-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T20:26:39-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"pi","terminal":"9f620892"}}
{"id":"sidx-close","parent":"search-index","ord":"a3","title":"address + CI once + AUTO-MERGE on green (approved 20:14)","done":"2026-08-24T21:33:02-04:00","desc":"Closed 21:34. All four folds at 814e198c: (1) MEMORY measured — 291 bytes per indexed record/document on the long-lived Bun heap (the brainstorm's ~3×-text disk estimate holds in RAM too) — in the bench, README and PR body; (2) the soak crosses CROWD_FLOOR both ways in phases (write mix biased per phase, planted selectivity words, both answers compared every round, each phase asserts the decision FLIPPED; the constant exported so phases read the real value); (3) the seven traced shapes generated with non-zero counters — a shape that stops being reachable FAILS rather than shrinking coverage; (4) both NITs. Self-caught regression fixed (the phased soak was 5× the repo's slowest test and timed out under the parallel suite — 814e198c makes the superset check one expect and states a 30s hang backstop; back to ~3s, green twice). Mutation checks prove coverage bites (dropping arms fails counts). Master merged on a real conflict (4e089dc3, the ops row — the one CLAUDE.md condition). Load-honesty: quiet vs loadavg-37 numbers both stated, ratios held, memory byte-identical. Bar: 16/16 typecheck, 3655/0 + 77 twice; CI 10/10 @ 814e198c, e2e 930/8080. MERGED 90460125 (squash) on the human's 20:14 approval + 20:15 automerge; worktree removed, branch deleted, terminal a41b4aac retired.","after":["sidx-review-grok","sidx-review-pi"],"created":"2026-08-24T19:02:23-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T21:33:02-04:00"}
{"id":"pldb-implement","parent":"perf-list-documents-bytes","ord":"a0","title":"implement + differential test + bench + open PR","done":"2026-08-24T20:54:17-04:00","desc":"Reported 20:52 (terminal 1d169bd6, 15m4s): PR #375 @ 665868fe — the listing reports entry.bytes remembered where the store holds the body, instead of bytesOf(entry.body) per document at query.ts. Differential test over the suite corpus + a generated multi-byte corpus; the classic failure pinned (bytesOf(\"👋\")=4 vs .length=2). Bench (5k docs, 5.77MB, emoji on a seventh): 4.69ms → 0.79ms median-of-9, arms must answer identically or the run fails — 5.9×. e2e untouched (answers byte-identical). Remaining per-call walk cost named on the roadmap node, out of scope. Bar: 15/15 typecheck, 3651/0 + 77 unit. CI correctly deferred to close. No deferrals.","created":"2026-08-24T20:37:14-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T20:54:17-04:00","custom":{"pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/375 @ 665868fe","terminal":"1d169bd6"}}
{"id":"pldb-review-pi","parent":"perf-list-documents-bytes","ord":"a1","title":"review: pi (split)","done":"2026-08-24T20:58:51-04:00","desc":"pi, DO-NOT-OBJECT, 0 MUST, 0 SHOULD, 1 NIT, at 665868fe (20:58, ~4m, by reading) — https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/375#issuecomment-5403559273. Verified with receipts: STALENESS clean — bodiedDocument (document.ts:421) is the ONLY Markdown construction site (grepped every kind), and write (following.ts:128), external edits/git pulls (codec.ts:60 via probe re-read), create and rename all funnel through it, so bytes recomputes alongside body; no serialized boundary decodes old Documents (no migration hazard). One-truth: bytesOf (documents.ts:450) sole definition, one call feeding the field. Differential: suite corpus walks the real fixtures; generated corpus covers astral plane, ZWJ, combining marks, CJK, frontmatter-with-emoji; torn-file interplay handled. Bench: alternating warms, median-of-9, JSON-compares whole listings before timing. NIT: differential is cold-listing only — a write→relist case would pin the single-constructor property.","after":["pldb-implement"],"created":"2026-08-24T20:37:14-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T20:58:51-04:00","custom":{"reviewer":"pi","terminal":"8ed6a3a6"}}
{"id":"pldb-close","parent":"perf-list-documents-bytes","ord":"a2","title":"address + CI once + AUTO-MERGE on green","done":"2026-08-24T22:06:26-04:00","desc":"Closed 22:07. The NIT fold (write→relist differential) and then the #374 conflict merge at 3b3e354f: bodiedDocument stays the ONLY Markdown constructor (index rebuild and listing share one decode; a write refreshes bytes as it re-folds the body the index indexes), and #374's write-gate soak now ALSO asserts listing-sizes ≡ recompute after every write incl. write_document/create_document — the two differentials compose. Bar at the merged head: 16/16 typecheck, 3661/0 + 77, documents.feature 32/32. CI: first run 9/10 (unrelated e2e flake in the_conversations_servers.feature — ledgered), e2e rerun 930/930, all green. MERGED 0c71691b (squash); worktree removed, branch deleted, terminal 1d169bd6 retired.","after":["pldb-review-pi"],"created":"2026-08-24T20:37:14-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T22:06:26-04:00"}
