{"id":"perf-validate-flip","parent":"psw2-model","ord":"a7","title":"Flip the incremental validator authoritative — one line, merge=HUMAN","todo":true,"desc":"The narrowed validator runs as a SHADOW since #383. This is the one line in format/src/validate.ts that makes its verdict the answer, and the removal of the full arm from the write path.\n\n- Merge is a HUMAN's: behaviour is what changes here — the shadow PR's whole argument was that nothing did.\n- GATE, machine-checkable: $XDG_STATE_HOME/olai/validate-shadow.ndjson empty or absent (the path is the writer's own exported constant — #383's fold pinned the agreement after grok caught the gate naming a file the process never writes), AND ≥3 quiet nights of soak. A non-empty log freezes the flip — a divergence is the shadow doing its one job; 'it looks benign' is not a reading anybody may take.\n- TIME-BOUNDED: flip or remove within 7 days; default on the deadline is REMOVE (shadow.ts and its call go, the divergence wiring with them). Either way incremental.ts, its test/testlib and the bench STAY — the harness is the durable artifact.\n- Divergence alarms surface in the orchestrator's morning summary.","created":"2026-08-25T01:58:25-04:00","custom":{"dispatch-trigger":"the shadow's soak: divergence log ($XDG_STATE_HOME/olai/validate-shadow.ndjson) empty-or-absent ∧ ≥3 quiet nights, within 7 days of the shadow landing; a NON-EMPTY log FREEZES this. Merge=HUMAN, never an agent's","from":"the converged nightly plan (perf-sweep nightly-plan prop) + #383's shadow"}}
